{
  "note": [
    "The Upper Elevator's fabric (DR-113), cut from the one tower layout in scripts/fabric-tower.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. UPPER-ELEVATOR.metadata.json v4: a 3.8 x 3.1 x 3.4 car, the eye at the middle, ONE hole 2.2 x 2.5 in its south wall, which SOUTH and OUT are both names for (compone.zil 2393-2394). Its south wall stands against the Tower Core's drum, which is where 3.4 + 0.12 + 0.08 + 1.7 puts its eye 5.30 m north of the core's axis.",
    "TWO landings through that one hole, chosen by UPPER-ELEVATOR-UP, so both are here and each is hung on the global. Up (the state the game starts in, compone.zil 2599): the Tower Core's own fabric -- the curved concrete wall and worn floor, the far wall 8.5 m off, the stair at drum x -2.2 and, past it, the south-west gap with the Observation Deck's daylight and the sea beyond the parapet. Down: the Elevator Lobby, which is fabric-kalamontee.mjs's room and not this file's -- it is built here only as this car's other glimpse, from the numbers this package states (12 x 3.8 x 10, this 2.2 x 2.5 hole in its north wall, the 3.4 x 3 red door in its far wall 11.86 m off with the red button 2.1 m east of its centre). Neither the Corridor Junction mouth nor the Booth 2 mouth is drawn: both are behind the jambs.",
    "The states this eye can see: the blue door shut (its leaf is drawn on whichever side the car is standing at, so there is never a second leaf); the slot lit once the card is accepted, which in this port is permanent; and the lobby's far red door, open only while the Lower Elevator is up with its own door open -- the one thing in that glimpse that changes, and the reason it is here rather than painted shut."
